Ahem was developed by Todd Fahrner and Myles C. Maxfield.
W3C declares Ahem public domain, with a Creative Commons Zero declaration where applicable:
https://www.w3.org/Style/CSS/Test/Fonts/Ahem/

This unmodified font is sourced from Web Platform Tests:
https://github.com/web-platform-tests/wpt/blob/master/fonts/Ahem.ttf
Source blob: 4d4785a4123287a5ca08439a6230514de91df0e7

It is a regression-testing font. Most glyphs intentionally render as boxes.
